<title>USA: Colombia eyeing global bond - NY syndicate sources.</title>
<headline>Colombia eyeing global bond - NY syndicate sources.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia is expected to issue $750 million to $1.0 billion in global bonds in coming weeks through Merrill Lynch &amp; Co and J.P. Morgan Securities, said debt syndicate sources.</p>
<p>Sources noted, however, that the maturity and the specific amount has not yet been decided.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch and J.P. Morgan declined comment.</p>
</text>
